Interpretation guidance:
  If drift direction and age-group ordering are consistent across
  panels, this confirms that the headline results are not driven by
  rural/urban composition.
  Larger absolute magnitudes in city-restricted panels are expected
  because rural individuals (who have less spatial expansion) are
  progressively excluded.

Note on non-nested strata:
  Truly non-nested strata (rural-only, small-urban-only, etc.) would
  require re-running step2_kernel_generation.R on raw microdata with
  stratum-specific filters. These results use the best evidence
  available from the shared kernel artifacts.


